      <text:p text:style-name="P23"/>
      <text:p text:style-name="P23">Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure1" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2</text:sequence>: A Cellular System Architecture</text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1" text:is-list-header="true"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8241_791065363"/>Cell Anatomy<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8241_791065363"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P16"><text:span text:style-name="T88">Each cell contains one or more </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T17">A</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20">ctivators</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T88"> that evaluate stimuli as they arrive. <text:s/>Activators </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89">process stimuli on their </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T17">R</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21">eceptors</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> and advertise </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T90">new</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T89"> stimuli on their </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T17">T</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21">ransmitters </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T35">(see Figure </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T39">3</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T88">.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T138">)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T88"> <text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T106">Each activator has its own set of receptors, transmitters and subscriptions. <text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T107">The names of receptors </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T154">and transmitters </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T107">are not required to be unique among a cell’s activators; activators can share receptors </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T154">and transmitters </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T107">as long as they agree on the stimulus type.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2" text:is-list-header="true"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8251_791065363"/>Receptors<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8251_791065363"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="T91">R</text:span>eceptors are named, type-safe receptacles for stimuli. <text:s/><text:span text:style-name="T117">They consume stimuli that satisfy a subscription.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2" text:is-list-header="true"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8253_791065363"/>Transmitters<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc8253_791065363"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="T91">T</text:span>ransmitters are named, type-safe emitters of stimuli. <text:s/><text:span text:style-name="T117">They forward stimuli to </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T118">interested </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T117">synapses.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P25" text:outline-level="2" text:is-list-header="true"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Frame2" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="0.0008in" svg:y="0.1256in" svg:width="6.6165in" draw:z-index="4">
